.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt OTELPFD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm otelpfd
.Nd export pf statistics as OpenTelemetry metrics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar count
.Op Fl e Ar endpoint
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl i Ar interval
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the
.Xr pf 4
status with the
.Dv DIOCGETSTATUS
ioctl, the structure that
.Ql pfctl -s info
prints, every
.Ar interval
seconds and sends it as OTLP metrics to the endpoint configured in
.Xr otel.conf 5 .
It is normally started by the
.Pa otelpfd
rc.d script; see
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-e endpoint"
.It Fl c Ar count
Exit after
.Ar count
samples.
By default
.Nm
runs until it receives
.Dv SIGTERM ,
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGHUP ,
then flushes pending metrics and exits.
.It Fl e Ar endpoint
Send to
.Ar endpoint
instead of the one resolved from the environment and
.Xr otel.conf 5 .
Credentials from the
.Xr otel.conf 5
headers file are not sent to it.
.It Fl f Ar file
Read consecutive binary
.Vt struct pf_status
records from
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa /dev/pf ,
and stop at its end.
This replays captured samples for testing and diagnosis.
.It Fl i Ar interval
Seconds between samples, 0.1 to 3600; the default is 15.
.It Fl u Ar user
After opening
.Pa /dev/pf
and reading the configuration, switch permanently to
.Ar user .
.El
.Sh METRICS
Names carry the
.Dq Ar service . Ns Li pf.
prefix of the exporter, where
.Ar service
is
.Dq otelpfd
unless
.Ev OTEL_SERVICE_NAME
says otherwise.
.Bl -tag -width "src_node_operations"
.It Li running , states , states_halfopen , src_nodes , fragments , syncookies_active
Gauges.
.It Li state_operations , src_node_operations , fragment_operations
Cumulative sums by
.Va operation
.Pq search, insert, removal .
.It Li reasons
Cumulative sums by
.Va reason ,
the pf drop and match reason counters.
.It Li limits
Cumulative sums by
.Va limit ,
the limit counters.
.It Li packets
Cumulative sums by
.Va network.type
.Pq inet, inet6 ,
.Va direction
.Pq in, out
and
.Va action
.Pq pass, block .
.It Li bytes
Cumulative sums by
.Va network.type
and
.Va direction .
.El
.Sh SECURITY
.Pa /dev/pf
is opened read-only and its capability rights are limited to the single
.Dv DIOCGETSTATUS
ioctl before the process changes to
.Ar user .
.Nm
does not enter capability mode because its exporter must be able to
connect to the collector again after a failure.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors exit 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr otel.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr otelconf 8 ,
.Xr pfctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
